# What Docker must not send to the daemon.
#
# node_modules is the important line. It is ~90MB of host-built packages, some
# with native binaries compiled for macOS, and the builder runs `npm ci` to
# install the same lock file for Linux -- so sending it is slow and wrong at
# the same time.
#
# The secret patterns are here for the same reason as in the backend context:
# the Dockerfile copies by name today, and this is the second defence for the
# day somebody changes that.

# Secrets. Vite inlines VITE_ variables into the bundle, so a .env reaching
# this context is not only a file in an image -- it is a value published to
# every browser that loads the app.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example

# Installed and built output. Both are produced inside the builder.
node_modules/
dist/

# Test and tooling state.
coverage/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Version control and editor state.
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
